Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> In my last game on Astral I was quite immediately surrounded by three
> purple L's, two arch-liches and a master lich. I killed them the usual
> way, nothing exciting. But I remember that recently it was mentioned
> that one could tame undead creatures using The Book. Would The Book be
> effective with such high level beasts? (Though I suppose the liches'
> "magic resistance" prevents successful taming.) It didn't come to my
> mind at that moment anyway, but it would have been cool to tame three
> major liches with a single reciting of The Book.

Monsters don't get saving throws against the Book's taming: if they're
in range, undead, co-aligned with you, and otherwise tameable, they
get tamed. It's that last criterion that arch-liches and master liches
will always fail on; they're covetous, and covetous monsters can't be
tamed. (They will be made peaceful, though.)

